<!-- DESIGN DECISIONS TABLE — key choices made in this module -->
<h2>&#127959;&#65039; Design Decisions</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Decision</th><th>Choice Made</th><th>Alternatives Considered</th><th>Why This Approach</th></tr>
  <table>
      <tr><th>Decision</th><th>Choice Made</th><th>Alternatives Considered</th><th>Why This Approach</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Hybrid Retrieval</td><td>40% BM25 + 60% dense + graph</td><td>Pure keyword, pure semantic, pure graph</td><td>Keyword catches exact matches (high precision), dense catches semantic shifts (high recall), graph adds reasoning. Weighted combination balances all three.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Chunking Strategy</td><td>14 document-type handlers</td><td>Single generic chunker, no structure</td><td>Different document types (PDFs, tables, code, books, emails) have different natural breakpoints. Type-aware chunking preserves semantics and table structure.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>RAPTOR for Summarization</td><td>Recursive clustering + LLM summarization</td><td>Simple truncation, single-level summarization</td><td>Preserves hierarchical meaning. When context is huge, RAPTOR recursively builds a summary tree, letting the LLM see both detail and overview without token explosion.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Entity Graph</td><td>Leiden community detection + LLM extraction</td><td>No entity reasoning, simple keyword co-occurrence</td><td>Leiden's stochastic optimization finds natural entity clusters without hardcoded rules. LLM extracts relationships with reasoning. Graph enables cross-document reasoning.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Storage Abstraction</td><td>Factory pattern with 10+ backends</td><td>Single hard-coded storage backend</td><td>Users may deploy to S3, MinIO, Azure, GCS, or on-prem OpenDAL. Abstraction prevents vendor lock-in and allows switching without code changes.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Background Task Execution</td><td>Redis-coordinated task queues (SVR)</td><td>Synchronous indexing, thread pool</td><td>Indexing can be slow (millions of docs). Redis coordination allows distributed workers. Async indexing doesn't block the API.</td></tr>
    </table>

