<!-- WHAT COULD GO WRONG — failure modes and how the module handles them -->
<h2>&#9888;&#65039; What Could Go Wrong</h2>
<table>
      <tr><th>Failure Mode</th><th>Trigger</th><th>Detection</th><th>Recovery / Mitigation</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Empty result set</td><td>Query has no keyword or semantic matches in index</td><td>Fusion returns 0 results or all scores below threshold</td><td>Return empty results with explanation. Suggest clarifying query or expanding search scope. Log for analytics to find indexing gaps.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Embedding model unavailable</td><td>Embedding service (local ONNX, remote API) is down</td><td>HTTP 503 or connection timeout on embedding call</td><td>Fall back to keyword-only search (BM25). This degrades recall but preserves functionality. Alert ops team.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Entity graph corruption</td><td>Graph database inconsistency after partial update</td><td>Entity lookup returns contradictory relationships or infinite loops</td><td>Skip entity graph signal for this request. Cache hit rate drops but system doesn't crash. Trigger async graph repair job.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Context explosion from RAPTOR</td><td>Summarization LLM calls fail or are very slow with huge inputs</td><td>RAPTOR tree-building takes >10 seconds or hits token limit</td><td>Stop RAPTOR recursion early, return best current summary node. Degrade gracefully rather than timeout.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Stale index / write-read consistency</td><td>New documents indexed but not yet searchable; query issued before index propagates</td><td>User reports "I just uploaded a doc but it doesn't show up in results"</td><td>Add index refresh delay (eventual consistency model). Offer explicit "refresh index" endpoint for impatient users.</td></tr>
    </table>

<!-- PERFORMANCE PROFILE — where time and memory are spent -->
<h2>&#9889; Performance Profile</h2>
<div style="background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:1.4rem 1.6rem;margin:1.5rem 0;">
<h3 style="margin-top:0;">Hot Paths</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>BM25 search:</strong> O(log n) inverted index lookup per query term. Typically 5–20ms for 1M-document corpus. Dominates when query is very selective (few matching docs).</li>
  <li><strong>Dense embedding search:</strong> O(n) or O(log n) depending on index type (linear for brute-force, logarithmic for HNSW/IVF). 20–100ms for 1M vectors. Dominates when query has semantic shifts.</li>
  <li><strong>Fusion & ranking:</strong> O(k log k) where k = number of returned candidates (typically 100–500). <5ms. Negligible compared to search.</li>
  <li><strong>RAPTOR summarization (optional):</strong> O(n log n) for clustering + O(log n) LLM calls (tree depth). Only triggered for large result sets. 1–5 seconds but runs offline if possible.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Resource Usage</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Memory:</strong> Embedding indices live in-memory (e.g., HNSW graph). A 1M-document corpus with 768-dim embeddings ≈ 3GB. Chunking buffers are temporary (freed after indexing).</li>
  <li><strong>I/O:</strong> BM25 index stored on disk (typically 10–20% of chunk data size). Accessed via memory-mapped files. Minimal I/O except during index rebuild (background job via SVR).</li>
  <li><strong>Network:</strong> If embedding model is remote (e.g., OpenAI API), adds 500ms–2s latency per query. Consider local ONNX models for privacy and speed.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<!-- SUB-MODULE CARDS — one per sub-module, link to submod/index.html -->
<h2>Sub-Modules</h2>
<div class="card-grid">
      <a title="RAG app — Document Chunking (14 Types)" class="card" href="app/index.html">
        <h4>app/</h4>
        <p>Multi-format document chunking strategies.</p>
        <ul><li>14 chunker implementations</li><li>Format-aware semantic boundaries</li><li>Preserve table & code structure</li></ul>
      </a>
      <a title="RAG flow — Pipeline Orchestration" class="card" href="flow/index.html">
        <h4>flow/</h4>
        <p>DAG-based retrieval pipeline orchestration.</p>
        <ul><li>Graph execution engine</li><li>Pluggable chunker selection</li><li>Parser & extractor framework</li></ul>
      </a>
      <a title="RAG nlp — Tokenization &amp; Query Analysis" class="card" href="nlp/index.html">
        <h4>nlp/</h4>
        <p>Tokenization, query analysis, term weighting.</p>
        <ul><li>DART trie tokenizer (Rust FFI)</li><li>CJK-aware segmentation</li><li>Query synonym expansion</li></ul>
      </a>
      <a title="RAG llm — LLM Provider Abstraction" class="card" href="llm/index.html">
        <h4>llm/</h4>
        <p>Multi-provider LLM adapters and embeddings.</p>
        <ul><li>Chat, embedding, reranking models</li><li>Vision (OCR, CV) support</li><li>Provider abstraction</li></ul>
      </a>
      <a title="RAG graphrag — Entity Graphs &amp; Relationships" class="card" href="graphrag/index.html">
        <h4>graphrag/</h4>
        <p>Entity relationship extraction and reasoning.</p>
        <ul><li>Microsoft GraphRAG & LightRAG</li><li>Leiden community detection</li><li>Entity resolution & linking</li></ul>
      </a>
      <a title="RAG utils — Storage Backends &amp; Abstraction" class="card" href="utils/index.html">
        <h4>utils/</h4>
        <p>Storage abstraction and index backends.</p>
        <ul><li>10+ storage providers</li><li>Encryption & compression</li><li>Factory pattern for extensibility</li></ul>
      </a>
      <a title="RAG svr — Background Task Execution" class="card" href="svr/index.html">
        <h4>svr/</h4>
        <p>Background task execution and coordination.</p>
        <ul><li>Redis-backed task queues</li><li>Distributed indexing</li><li>Cache & sync services</li></ul>
      </a>
      <a title="RAG raptor — Hierarchical Recursive Summarization" class="card" href="raptor/index.html">
        <h4>raptor/</h4>
        <p>Hierarchical recursive summarization trees.</p>
        <ul><li>UMAP + Gaussian Mixture clustering</li><li>Multi-level LLM summarization</li><li>Tree traversal & compression</li></ul>
      </a>
    </div>

<!-- DIRECTORY MAP — module-level source tree -->
<h2 id="directory-map">Directory Map</h2>
<details open>
<summary style="cursor:pointer;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">Source tree for RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)</summary>
<pre style="background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1rem;margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.6;overflow-x:auto;"><code>rag/
├── app/                      ← 14 document-type chunkers (naive, paper, book, manual, presentation, qa, table, resume, picture, audio, email, tag, one, laws)
├── flow/                      ← DAG pipeline orchestration (pipeline.py, base.py, parser/, chunker/, extractor/)
├── nlp/                       ← Tokenization & query analysis (rag_tokenizer.py, search.py, query.py, term_weight.py, synonym.py)
├── llm/                       ← LLM adapters (chat, embedding, rerank, cv, ocr, sequence2txt, tts)
├── graphrag/                  ← Entity graphs & relationship extraction (general/, light/, leiden, entity_resolution, search)
├── utils/                     ← Storage backends (es/, infinity/, opensearch/, ob/, minio/, s3/, azure/, gcs/, oss/, opendal/, encrypted/)
├── svr/                       ← Background services (task_executor.py, cache_file_svr.py, sync_data_source.py, discord_svr.py)
├── raptor.py                  ← Hierarchical summarization (UMAP, GMM clustering, tree building)
└── __init__.py
</code></pre>
</details>

